* Foreign comment dialect: the parameter lines carry trailing `;` comments, the
* style used by HSPICE/Spectre and by every card in the lab's own
* SJTU-YONGFU-RESEARCH-GRP/spice_model_collections repository (whose files are
* advertised as "ready-to-use ... including NGSPICE").
*
* ngspice does not treat `;` as a comment. The token becomes `0.7;` and the
* card's whole parameter line dies in strtod with
*
*     strtod: Invalid argument
*
* This card must be REFUSED. A card that loads while meaning something other
* than what it says is the failure mode this channel exists to prevent.
.MODEL n1 NMOS LEVEL=1
+ VTO    = 0.7         ; Threshold voltage (V)
+ KP     = 50.0e-6     ; Transconductance parameter (A/V^2)
+ GAMMA  = 0.8         ; Bulk threshold parameter (V^0.5)
+ PHI    = 0.7         ; Surface potential (V)
+ LAMBDA = 0.02        ; Channel length modulation (1/V)
